# Everything in the repo is site content and gets served, EXCEPT what is listed
# here. Anything added to the repo that is not meant to be public — internal
# notes, build tooling, deploy config — must be added to this list.
#
# config/ is the one exception that stays in the context: the Dockerfile needs
# config/nginx.conf, and .dockerignore would put it out of reach. The Dockerfile
# deletes it from the served root instead.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.kamal
config/deploy.yml
docs
README.md
CONTENT-TODO.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
